  "body": "## What changed (part 1 of #3751: the `--ui` transport)\n\n- Each CamCraft window opens a UI link at start (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell_window.rs`). `CAMCRAFT_UI_LINK=off` starts a window without it.\n  - Linux and macOS: a Unix domain socket in the user's link folder (folder 0700, socket 0600).\n  - Windows: TCP on `127.0.0.1` only, with a port that the OS selects. std has no named pipe. The dependency question for a named pipe is on #3751.\n- The window writes a discovery file `<pid>.json` (pid, transport, address, token, open project, version) and removes it when it closes (`crates/app/src/mcp/link.rs`). The file follows the open project.\n- Each connection must send the token from the file first. Any other first line closes the connection before a line reaches the app.\n- The session speaks the MCP JSON-RPC of `camcraft-cli mcp`. The window answers each line in `mcp_host::pump` with `answer_live_with`, as for `--mcp-port`: on the UI thread, on the window's History, behind the same live gate. There is no second command set. Ctrl+Z undoes a CLI step.\n- New CLI lane `camcraft-cli --ui [--window <pid|project>] <verb>` (`crates/app/src/cli_ui.rs`, client in `crates/app/src/mcp/link_client.rs`):\n  - `call <tool> [<json-args>]`: one tool call; prints the tool's JSON; a refused tool exits 1.\n  - `mcp`: a stdio MCP bridge to the window.\n  - `windows`: lists the link files.\n- No window: a clear error (\"no running CamCraft window ... (nothing ran)\") and exit 3. The CLI never falls back to a headless document. Several windows without `--window`: a list and exit 2.\n- The listener of `--mcp-port` now serves a stream type that hides TCP or Unix (`crates/app/src/mcp/wire.rs`). `port_from` moved to `port_flag.rs` (400-line law). The behaviour of `--mcp-port` does not change.\n- No new dependency. The token comes from std's `RandomState` keys (seeded from the OS random source).\n\nDecision file: `docs/decisions/3751-cli-ui-link.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::tests::ui_link::a_cli_ui_call_shows_in_the_window_and_ctrl_z_removes_it` (camcraft-ui lib): the harness window opens its link; the `--ui` lane (`cli_ui::run_in`) sends `set_stock`, `add_tool`, `add_operation`; the browser shows `Face1`; Ctrl+Z removes it; a refused call exits 1; the link file goes with the window.\n- `mcp_live` / `ui_link::a_cli_call_with_no_window_says_so_and_exits_3`: the real `camcraft-cli` binary with an empty link folder, a stale file, and an unknown pid: exit 3, the message, nothing on stdout.\n- `mcp_live` / `ui_link::a_wrong_token_is_refused_and_the_window_goes_on_serving`: a wrong token is refused (exit code 1), no line reaches the app, and the next client with the right token is served.\n- `mcp_live` / `ui_link::bad_ui_arguments_are_usage_errors`, `the_link_file_follows_the_open_project`, `the_link_folder_is_the_users_own`.\n- `cli` / `every_subcommand_answers_help_and_names_its_flags` now walks the `--ui` lane too (`HELP_LANES`).\n\n## Readings\n\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6): 185 steps, 0 failed (`mcp_live` 19 passed, `cli` 13 passed, camcraft-ui lib 1584 passed).\n- Clippy `-D warnings`: camcraft-app (lib, bins, `mcp_live`, `cli`), camcraft-ui (lib, bins, lib tests).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The Unix socket arms (`#[cfg(unix)]`) were not compiled or run here: the work was on Windows. The post-merge runner (Linux) builds them.\n- No real window was started on the desktop. The UI test uses the harness only.\n- `--ui mcp` (the stdio bridge) has no test of its own; it uses the same `connect` as `--ui call`.\n- `script` and `process` do not take `--ui`. Follow-up: #3850.\n- Part 2 (`--skill <target> install`) is not in this PR.\n\nChangelog: `camcraft-cli --ui [--window <pid|project>] call <tool> [<json>]` (and `--ui mcp`, `--ui windows`) sends MCP tool calls to a running CamCraft window, which runs them on its own undo history; with no window it exits 3 and runs nothing.\n\nEffort: max\n\nRefs #3751\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
